course: dictionary
lesson: 11124
title: Who sells in bulk?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A wholesaler is a business that buys goods in large amounts from makers and sells them in large amounts to shops. It does not sell to the public. The example says, «Shops buy goods in large amounts from wholesalers, firms that sell in bulk to shops, and sell them at a higher price.» The key clue is the word bulk, which means large amounts.
explain: Think of the goods moving in steps: maker, then wholesaler, then shop, then you. The wholesaler buys in bulk, so it can sell cheaply. The shop pays the wholesaler, then sells the goods to people at a higher price.
explain: Profit is the money a shop keeps after paying for its goods. In maths, profit = shop price − wholesale price. If a shop pays £4 for a box of pencils and sells it for £6, its profit is £2.
fact: A wholesaler buys goods in large amounts (in bulk) from makers.
fact: A wholesaler sells in bulk to shops, not to members of the public.
fact: Shops are called retailers because they sell to people.
fact: «Wholesaler» means a person or business that sells in large amounts to shops.
fact: Profit = shop price − wholesale price.
exercise: «Shops buy goods in large amounts from wholesalers.» Who do wholesalers sell in bulk to? | Children at school | *Shops | Makers of the goods | Customers in the street
exercise: A wholesaler sells a box of pens to a shop for £5. The shop sells it for £8. What is the shop's profit? | £5 | £2 | *£3 | £13
exercise: Which word means a business that sells in large amounts to shops? | Bargain | Customer | Retailer | *Wholesaler
test: A wholesaler mainly sells to whom? | People buying one item at a time | Nobody at all | Children at home | *Shops
test: A wholesaler sells to a shop for £7. The shop sells the same goods for £10. What is the profit? | *£3 | £2 | £17 | £70
exam: A wholesaler buys 100 bags from a maker and sells them to a shop for £250. The shop sells them for £400. What is the shop's profit? | £250 | *£150 | £100 | £650
